From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:03:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: Request the reset GPIO only where a handler
 uses it

When onboard_usb_dev powers a WiFi/Bluetooth combo chip, the enable
line of the chip is the reset-gpios property of its USB device node,
and onboard_usb_dev holds that line. btusb asks for a "reset" GPIO on
the same node for every device and ends the probe on any error, so it
fails with -EBUSY and the Bluetooth function of the chip stays unbound.
Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S with an AIC8800D80: no hci0.

Only the reset handlers of Intel, MediaTek, QCA and Realtek devices
use the line. Request it for those devices only. For them nothing
changes, a failure to get the line still ends the probe. All other
devices never drove the line after probe. On a combo chip a btusb
reset through it would also cut the WiFi function.

A combo chip of one of these vendors behind onboard_usb_dev still
collides; that needs the reset to go through onboard_usb_dev.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with onboard_usb_dev holding the CHIP_EN line of
the AIC8800D80, btusb binds the Bluetooth interfaces and hci0 comes up,
WiFi on the same chip keeps working.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c | 22 +++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
index ece1fd426f12..c842e03f079e 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -4301,13 +4301,21 @@ static int btusb_probe(struct usb_interface *intf,
 
 	SET_HCIDEV_DEV(hdev, &intf->dev);
 
-	reset_gpio = gpiod_get_optional(&data->udev->dev, "reset",
-					GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
-	if (IS_ERR(reset_gpio)) {
-		err = PTR_ERR(reset_gpio);
-		goto err_free_hdev;
-	} else if (reset_gpio) {
-		data->reset_gpio = reset_gpio;
+	/* Only the Intel, MediaTek, QCA and Realtek reset handlers use the
+	 * reset line. On other devices it may belong to another driver,
+	 * such as onboard_usb_dev powering a WiFi/Bluetooth combo chip.
+	 */
+	if (id->driver_info & (BTUSB_INTEL_COMBINED | BTUSB_MEDIATEK |
+			       BTUSB_QCA_ROME | BTUSB_QCA_WCN6855 |
+			       BTUSB_REALTEK)) {
+		reset_gpio = gpiod_get_optional(&data->udev->dev, "reset",
+						GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+		if (IS_ERR(reset_gpio)) {
+			err = PTR_ERR(reset_gpio);
+			goto err_free_hdev;
+		} else if (reset_gpio) {
+			data->reset_gpio = reset_gpio;
+		}
 	}
 
 	hdev->open    = btusb_open;
